  </section>

  <!-- In-Depth Clinical Guide: Wisdom Tooth Extraction in Hennur -->
  <section class="py-16 px-6 lg:px-24 bg-japandi-sand/25 border-y border-japandi-clay/30">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
      
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium tracking-tight">
          Comprehensive Guide to Wisdom Tooth Removal in Hennur, Bangalore
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Wisdom teeth (third molars) are the final permanent teeth to erupt into the oral cavity, typically emerging between the ages of 17 and 25. In modern human jaws, evolutionary dietary shifts have led to narrower dental arches, leaving insufficient room for these large molars to erupt upright into a functional chewing position. As a consequence, third molars frequently become impacted—trapped beneath the gums, tilted sideways against adjacent teeth, or lodged within the jawbone.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          At House of Dental on Horamavu Agara Road, our surgical philosophy centers on atraumatic, minimally invasive extraction. Rather than applying heavy mechanical leverage that can bruise bone and tissue, our surgeons utilize specialized micro-surgical instruments, precise digital sectioning, and motorized cold-saline cooling. This dramatically reduces tissue trauma, swelling, and post-operative discomfort, allowing you to resume your everyday schedule in 24 to 48 hours.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Common Impaction Types -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          4 Common Types of Wisdom Tooth Impaction We Treat
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Our digital RVG radiography accurately categorizes the exact anatomical angle of your third molar:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">1. Mesioangular Impaction</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              The tooth tilts forward toward the front of the mouth at a 45-degree angle, pressing directly into the root or crown of the adjacent second molar. This is the most common impaction type, frequently trapping food particles and causing undetected caries in healthy teeth.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">2. Horizontal Impaction</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              The molar lies completely on its side at a 90-degree angle, buried beneath the gum and alveolar bone. As it attempts to erupt, it exerts intense pressure against the neighboring molar's roots, leading to severe localized neuralgic pain and bone resorption.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">3. Vertical Impaction</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              The tooth is oriented in a normal upright direction but is unable to fully clear the gum line due to insufficient jawbone length. The overlying flap of gum tissue (operculum) repeatedly traps food and bacteria, triggering acute pericoronitis infections.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">4. Distoangular Impaction</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              The tooth tilts backward toward the ascending ramus of the lower jawbone. This challenging impaction often requires specialized surgical bone contouring and careful sectioning to protect adjacent anatomical structures like the inferior alveolar nerve canal.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Warning Signs: When You Must Remove a Wisdom Tooth -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          Warning Signs That Demand Prompt Wisdom Tooth Evaluation
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Ignoring an impacted or infected wisdom tooth can lead to dangerous deep-space facial infections. Schedule an immediate consultation if you experience:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-japandi-sand/30 border border-japandi-clay/30 space-y-1.5">
            <span class="font-semibold text-japandi-moss uppercase text-[10px] tracking-wider block">Throbbing Jaw &amp; Ear Pain</span>
            <p>Persistent radiating pain extending from the back of the lower jaw up into the ear, temple, or neck.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-japandi-sand/30 border border-japandi-clay/30 space-y-1.5">
            <span class="font-semibold text-japandi-moss uppercase text-[10px] tracking-wider block">Swollen Gums &amp; Pericoronitis</span>
            <p>Red, inflamed, bleeding gum tissue behind the last molar that hurts when chewing or brushing.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-japandi-sand/30 border border-japandi-clay/30 space-y-1.5">
            <span class="font-semibold text-japandi-moss uppercase text-[10px] tracking-wider block">Trismus (Difficulty Opening Mouth)</span>
            <p>Stiffness in the masticatory muscles making it painful to open your mouth wide or swallow comfortably.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-japandi-sand/30 border border-japandi-clay/30 space-y-1.5">
            <span class="font-semibold text-japandi-moss uppercase text-[10px] tracking-wider block">Halitosis &amp; Foul Taste</span>
            <p>Chronic bad breath and an unpleasant metallic or sour taste caused by pus or food decomposing under the gum flap.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- The Atraumatic Surgical Procedure -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          The 4-Stage Atraumatic Removal Protocol at House of Dental
        </h3>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Stage 1: RVG Radiographic Nerve Mapping</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              We capture digital low-radiation RVG radiographs to precisely locate the position of your wisdom tooth roots relative to the inferior alveolar nerve canal and maxillary sinus.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Stage 2: Computerized Profound Local Anesthesia</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              We buffer the local anesthetic to match body pH and administer it with micro-gauge needles, rendering the tooth, bone, and surrounding gums 100% numb with zero injection sting.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Stage 3: Micro-Sectioning &amp; Gentle Extraction</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              Rather than forcing the tooth out whole, our surgeons section the crown into small fragments under continuous saline irrigation. Each section is lifted out effortlessly without straining the jaw.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Stage 4: Socket Cleansing &amp; Resorbable Suturing</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              The socket is thoroughly debrided with antiseptic irrigation and a collagen plug or PRF (platelet-rich fibrin) clot stabilizer is placed. Dissolvable micro-sutures seal the gums cleanly.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Recovery & Dry Socket Prevention -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          Post-Extraction Recovery &amp; How to Prevent Dry Socket
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Following our simple 48-hour recovery rules ensures smooth, painless healing with zero complications:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <span class="font-semibold text-japandi-moss uppercase text-[10px] tracking-wider block">Do's: Promote Healing</span>
            <ul class="space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
              <li>Keep firm biting pressure on the sterile gauze pack for 45 to 60 minutes after surgery.</li>
              <li>Apply cold ice packs to the outside of your cheek (15 mins on, 15 mins off) for the first 24 hours.</li>
              <li>Eat soft, cool foods like yogurt, ice cream, smoothies (eaten with a spoon), dal, and khichdi.</li>
              <li>Take prescribed pain-relieving anti-inflammatory medication before numbness wears off.</li>
              <li>Begin gentle warm salt water rinses 24 hours after surgery (after every meal).</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-japandi-sand/40 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <span class="font-semibold text-japandi-clay uppercase text-[10px] tracking-wider block">Don'ts: Prevent Dry Socket</span>
            <ul class="space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
              <li><strong>Do NOT use drinking straws:</strong> The suction dislodges the protective blood clot.</li>
              <li><strong>Do NOT smoke or use tobacco:</strong> Nicotine impairs capillary blood flow and delays bone healing.</li>
              <li><strong>Do NOT spit vigorously:</strong> Swallow saliva gently; spitting creates pressure in the mouth.</li>
              <li><strong>Do NOT touch the socket:</strong> Keep your tongue and fingers away from the surgical area.</li>
              <li><strong>Avoid hot, spicy, or crunchy foods:</strong> Chips, seeds, and hot curries irritate the raw gums.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Cost Breakdown Table Section -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          Transparent Wisdom Tooth Removal Cost in Hennur, Bangalore
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          At House of Dental, we maintain an ethical fee structure with zero surprise surcharges:
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-japandi-clay/40 bg-japandi-sand/30">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
            <thead class="bg-japandi-sand/80 text-japandi-charcoal font-medium border-b border-japandi-clay/40">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-4">Impaction Category</th>
                <th class="p-4">Surgical Complexity</th>
                <th class="p-4">Estimated Fee Range</th>
                <th class="p-4">Anesthesia Protocol</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-japandi-clay/20">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Erupted Third Molar</td>
                <td class="p-4">Simple non-surgical extraction</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹3,500 – ₹5,000</td>
                <td class="p-4">Computerized Local Anesthesia</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Soft Tissue Impaction</td>
                <td class="p-4">Minor flap elevation + extraction</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹5,000 – ₹7,000</td>
                <td class="p-4">Buffered Local Numbing</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Partial Bony Impaction</td>
                <td class="p-4">Bone troughing + tooth sectioning</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹6,500 – ₹8,000</td>
                <td class="p-4">Profound Local Block + PRF</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Full Horizontal / Deep Bony</td>
                <td class="p-4">Complex micro-surgical sectioning</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹7,500 – ₹9,000</td>
                <td class="p-4">Advanced Local Block + Suturing</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Local Catchment & Transit Directions -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          Emergency Wisdom Tooth Care Across Hennur &amp; North Bangalore
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Acute third molar pain strikes without warning. Located at 2nd Floor, SLV Nilaya, Horamavu Agara Road (beside Nayara Petrol Bunk), House of Dental is rapidly accessible across North-East Bangalore:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth space-y-1.5 font-light">
          <li><strong>Hennur Bande &amp; Geddalahalli:</strong> 2 to 5 minutes by car or two-wheeler.</li>
          <li><strong>Horamavu, Babusapalya &amp; Kalkere:</strong> 5 to 7 minutes via local corridors.</li>
          <li><strong>Kalyan Nagar, HRBR Layout &amp; Kammanahalli:</strong> 10 minutes via Hennur Road.</li>
